# Local scratch and run output. The example specs save their runs under
# examples/scratch/; none of it is part of the package.
scratch/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# Build. The extension is compiled by scikit-build-core from CMakeLists.txt.
build/
dist/
_skbuild/
*.so

# Caches the toolchain can be pointed at beside the source: the ffcx/dolfinx JIT,
# and matplotlib when MPLCONFIGDIR is set here to keep a run reproducible.
.jitcache*/
.mplconfig/

# Logs, wherever a run writes one.
*.log

# macOS and editors
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# Meshes. A run generates its mesh from the geometry file and archives it in its
# own directory, so a mesh anywhere else is a leftover. The geometry file is not
# ignored: it is small, and it is the record of where the inclusions were.
*.xdmf
*.h5

# The biarc refit of a CAD source, and the report that doubles as its cache key.
# fit_step_to_arcs derives both from the .step the geometry names, which is
# tracked and is the record; these are what a tolerance produced from it, and a
# different tolerance produces different ones. The .json carries the key the next
# call compares against, so keeping it is worth roughly seven seconds a run and
# nothing else. Deriving them again needs only the source and the parameters that
# are already in the geometry file, and a run archive copies whatever it actually
# used (fit_outputs), so nothing downstream depends on these being in the tree.
*_fit.step
*_fit.json

# Frames a movie render was part way through. visualize.phases_movie renders into one
# of these beside its output -- same filesystem, so the finished file lands by
# rename rather than by copy -- and removes it on the way out, including when the
# encode fails. What it cannot survive is the process being killed, which leaves
# a directory of PNGs that is large, worthless, and next to a run.
.ovpsolver-movie-*/
